{
 "esm": "1.1.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "SemiringReduce",
  "description": "Non-'+' reductions (spec \u00a73.5): a running max of c\u00b2 (j <= i; the first argmax takes the derivative), a scalar min observed cmin = min_j c[j] read as a factor (a nested min), a suffix product of (1 - c[j]) (j >= i; exclusion products, no division), a level search kap = min{k : c[k] > 0.3} used as a subscript c[kap] (one-hot over the axis, its own derivative zero), and a max_product semiring whose column e[i] reads no contracted index."
 },
